#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# function_convexity

#% text
# `function_convexity(f, x)` gives `1` when `f` is convex on its domain, `-1` when concave, `0` when linear, and `indeterminate` otherwise.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# It is the sign of the second derivative on the domain of `f` (see `function_sign`).

#% item
# Functions with kinks or jumps, such as `abs` and `floor`, are decided from the slopes between neighbouring sample points, since their second derivative misses the kinks.

#% item
# `function_convexity([f, cond], x)` restricts the domain.

#% item
# In several variables the principal minors of the Hessian decide: all `>= 0` for convex, of alternating sign for concave (`strict_inequalities: true`: strictly).

#% item
# With parameters `conditional_expression(1, c)`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# A parabola and a cubic:

#% cell
function_convexity(x^2, x)
#% output
#= 1

#% cell
function_convexity(x^3, x)
#% output
#= indeterminate

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# The logarithm is concave on its domain:

#% cell
function_convexity([log(x), x > 0], x)
#% output
#= -1

#% text
# A linear function:

#% cell
function_convexity(3*x + 1, x)
#% output
#= 0

#% text
# A cubic on half the line:

#% cell
function_convexity([x^3, x > 0], x)
#% output
#= 1

#% text
# A kink is convex:

#% cell
function_convexity(abs(x), x)
#% output
#= 1

#% subsection
# Options

#% text
# Two variables:

#% cell
[function_convexity(x^2 + y^2, [x, y]), function_convexity(x^2 - y^2, [x, y]), function_convexity(-exp(x + y), [x, y])]
#% output
#= [1, indeterminate, -1]

#% text
# Parameters:

#% cell
function_convexity(x^2 + a*x*y + y^2, [x, y])
#% output
#= conditional_expression(1, -2 <= a and a <= 2)

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The sign of the second derivative:

#% cell
function_sign(d(exp(x), [x, 2]), x)
#% output
#= 1

#% cell
function_convexity(exp(x), x)
#% output
#= 1

#% text
# A convex function lies below its chords: the midpoint check at sample points for `exp`:

#% cell
map(t => exp((t + 3)/2) <= (exp(t) + exp(3))/2, [-2, 0, 1, 2.5])
#% output
#= [true, true, true, true]

#% subsection
# Possible issues

#% text
# The same for the square root, and an unknown function stays unevaluated:

#% cell
[function_convexity(sqrt(x), x), function_convexity([sqrt(x), x > 0], x), function_convexity(g(x), x)]
#% output
#= [indeterminate, -1, function_convexity(g(x), x)]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `function_sign`, `function_monotonicity`, `d`
